🎯 Key Takeaways
Python's collections module provides specialized container datatypes.
Counter makes counting elements easier.
defaultdict simplifies working with missing dictionary keys.
deque is useful when adding/removing elements from both ends.
namedtuple provides named fields while retaining tuple behavior.
ChainMap provides a single view over multiple mappings.
UserDict, UserList, and UserString can be used to build customized collection-like classes.
